ed a usable calibration_gap. The dv_headroom checks below are denominated on this same set, so a short control arm must refuse here rather than silently certify headroom over fewer cells than the criteria need.", "kind": "readiness", "measured": 8.0, "threshold": 8.0, "direction": "lower", "control": "intended = len(SEEDS) x len(CONDITIONS) = 8", "met": true}, {"name": "harm_head_action_sensitivity_present", "description": "Worst-cell mean |harm_logit(z,a1)-harm_logit(z,a2)| over a fixed probe batch and two distinct movement actions, measured after P1 training. This is the SAME statistic the load-bearing criteria route on (a difference of two harm logits at one state under two actions), not a magnitude proxy on a different component -- 993 asserted the FORWARD head's sensitivity at 17.9x over floor while the readout the criteria actually read was flat. An action-blind harm head makes causal_sig structurally zero in BOTH arms, so below-floor means substrate-not-ready.", "kind": "readiness", "measured": 0.11381933093070984, "threshold": 0.05, "direction": "lower", "control": "16-sample probe batch, actions 0 vs 1, worst cell across the 8 SEPARATED (control) cells of the full-grid set", "worst_merged_harm_action_sensitivity_diagnostic": 0.23883843421936035, "offending_cell": "DENSE_SEPARATED_seed303", "met": true}, {"name": "p1_harm_events_observed_per_condition", "description": "MIN(total P1 harm events summed over arms+seeds) across the two hazard-density conditions -- 993 red-team fix F7: a pooled floor let SPARSE's harm head train on near-zero labeled data while DENSE's volume masked it. Taking the min across conditions requires BOTH to have real coverage.", "kind": "readiness", "measured": 1616.0, "threshold": 10.0, "direction": "lower", "control": "dense=1616, sparse=1878 (full-grid cells)", "met": true}, {"kind_note": "floor_headroom = min(control calibration_gap) - 0.0 is exactly the room the MERGED arm has to FALL, which is what this suppression-direction criterion consumes. 0.0 is used as the floor because 'no hazard-conditional harm calibration at all' is the meaningful bottom; the logit difference is formally unbounded below, so this UNDERSTATES the available room and is therefore conservative. Design-time probe expectation: ~0.082 measured vs 0.06 required (~1.36x).", "name": "dv_headroom_margin_room_below_control", "kind": "dv_headroom", "measured": 0.2285701633410682, "threshold": 0.15, "direction": "lower", "dv_name": "calibration_gap", "achievable_statistic": "floor_headroom", "criterion_threshold": 0.15, "headroom_margin": 1.0, "n_control_values": 8, "headroom_ratio": 1.5238010889404547, "dv_bounds": [0.0, 1.0]}, {"kind_note": "The 2026-09-03 cluster autopsy's own table pairs 993's max |calibration_gap| (0.00152) against SEPARATED_SIGNAL_FLOOR (0.02) for a 13.1x shortfall, so max_abs is the sanctioned statistic for this non-degeneracy floor. Design-time probe expectation: ~0.215 measured vs 0.08 required (~2.68x).", "name": "dv_headroom_control_signal_floor_reachable", "kind": "dv_headroom", "measured": 0.7154595876455262, "threshold": 0.4, "direction": "lower", "dv_name": "calibration_gap", "achievable_statistic": "max_abs", "criterion_threshold": 0.2, "headroom_margin": 2.0, "n_control_values": 8, "headroom_ratio": 1.7886489691138154}], "combination_rule": "PASS iff C1_dense AND C2_sparse when BOTH conditions clear non-degeneracy; if only one condition clears it, outcome is that condition's criterion alone (label prefixed single_condition_only_partial_evidence); if neither clears it, unknown/non_degenerate=false. Each criterion additionally requires ALL 4 seeds to show MERGED<=SEPARATED (sign-consistency), not just a pooled mean margin. MARGIN=0.15 and SEPARATED_SIGNAL_FLOOR=0.2 are derived from the control arm's measured range (see the module docstring), and both are additionally gated at runtime by the dv_headroom preconditions H1/H2, which are evaluated over the SEPARATED cells BEFORE any MERGED cell is tra